            <ArticleTitle>Plasma cell granulomas in non-lipemic xanthomatosis: apparent induction by indomethacin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>489-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 71-year-old man with non-lipemic, generalized, plane xanthomas developed nodules and tumors within one month of starting indomethacin therapy. These enlarged and spread during 5 months of daily indomethacin but promptly and spontaneously involuted when the indomethacin was discontinued. Within 4 months, the nodules and tumors were completely gone. The process is viewed as an &quot;indoderma&quot;, i.e. a granulomatous drug reaction, analogous to an iododerma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
